From 2ff534d55880e3808c52218faa7200ee4dcdb74d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:50:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: preserve the parent node reference during child
 lookup

venus_add_video_core() passes dev->of_node as the starting point of
of_find_node_by_name(). That iterator consumes the starting node's
reference even if no matching node exists. The caller does not own an
extra reference, so checking the two codec children drops two references
to the Venus parent during each probe.

The first Raphael module test decoded a frame successfully, but reload
of the original driver reported of_node refcount underflow and failed
in kernfs_find_and_get_ns() through venus_add_dynamic_nodes(). The
unbalanced parent lookup can invalidate the parent's sysfs state when
references held by the dynamic children are released.

Use of_get_child_by_name() to search only the immediate children without
consuming the parent reference. Keep the existing of_node_put(enp) for
the acquired child. This also avoids treating a similarly named node
under another device as an existing Venus child.

The faulty lookup already exists in the fixed raphael-7.1 ab4ce59
baseline. This is a Linux OF ownership fix, not an Android HFI/DMA port.
Do not hide the refcount warnings or add NULL checks to kernfs instead.

Test the extracted driver function with the actual fixed-baseline OF
lookup/traversal helpers and host reference-count/changeset stubs. The
old function loses a parent reference and incorrectly accepts unrelated
nodes; the new function must preserve all acquired references on both
success and allocation/property failures. Hardware teardown still needs
validation from a clean boot; the previous hot-reload entry stays blocked.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index f460645af..bd5325915 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@ static int venus_add_video_core(struct venus_core *core, const char *node_name,
 	if (!node_name)
 		return 0;
 
-	enp = of_find_node_by_name(dev->of_node, node_name);
+	enp = of_get_child_by_name(dev->of_node, node_name);
 	if (enp) {
 		of_node_put(enp);
 		return 0;
-- 
